					<string name="Source">-- what&apos;s breaking now: if you add Z in between garbages G1 and G2, so you have G1 Z G2, and then delete G1 and G2, you end up with Z having no neighbors!
-- now you can never reach Z...  but it&apos;s worse than that-- if Z is the closest thing to you when you put down a temporary waypoint,
-- then Z has no neighbors, so the closestedge fcn will return nil for e2, which means that when addNeighbors is further called to link in the temp
-- waypoint, the dist function there will get a nil and try to index it and crash

-- what you need to change:  instead of adding and deleting waypoints everytime garbage objects appear (which could be crazy bad for like 1000 garbage objects at once anyways)
-- just find the closest garbage object and keep a single waypoint for it (so you will only have &quot;temporaryWayPoint&quot;, &quot;GarbageWayPoint&quot;, and normal waypoints)
-- this will solve all problems :)

-- can furthermore make garbage waypoint spawn on closest point on navmesh edge to garbage, so then will &quot;suck in&quot; the part in question instead of
-- romping around on other peoples&apos; baseplates (or trying to, if it&apos;s covered by walls forcing robot to not be able to get to part :&apos;( )

